# Every reach from compiled code into userdict, by enclosing function.
# Checked by tests/check-userdict-reach.sh: the set is compared exactly,
# so a new reach and a vanished one both fail until this file says so.
#
# userdict is the program's workspace. A driver or a piece of machinery
# that reads configuration out of it has made an ambient name in the
# program's namespace into a control channel, which is the defect class
# the device knobs were converted away from; and one that defines into
# it has put machinery where a program can shadow it. A line here is a
# deliberate decision that the reach is the program's own business:
#
#   xpost_create          copies the boot definitions userdict was built
#                         with into systemdict when the language is
#                         built from source, and hands the same handle
#                         to the recording of host settings; it runs
#                         before any program.
#   xpost_add_definitions is the documented channel by which an embedder
#                         or -D defines names for the program to read.
#                         Programs read them; the interpreter's own
#                         machinery does not.
#
xpost_interpreter.c xpost_add_definitions
xpost_interpreter.c xpost_create
